0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Z80
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-24).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Four switches, set in the EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CPM      0 = generic ROM build (KEY/CONOUT at fixed addresses)
0000                             ;             1 = CP/M 2.2 .COM file: loads the file named on the command line
0000                             ;    EDITOR   1 = with the line editor built in (see the end of this file):
0000                             ;                 the spec's suggested standard. It goes with either setting
0000                             ;                 of the other two.
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: the programmer is responsible)
0000                             ;             1 = starts with every variable at 0 and every word undefined,
0000                             ;                 and stops on every error in the spec's table (and Ctrl-C)
0000                             ;                 with a four-line report: the letter and the place as line
0000                             ;                 and column, the text there, and both stacks. See `error`.
0000                             ;    ANSI     what the console escapes of "$" (/00bbIC8= /| /` /~) do:
0000                             ;             1 = send ANSI (VT100) sequences through CONOUT
0000                             ;             0 = call the machine's own routines CONCLS, CONEOL, CONCUR and
0000                             ;                 CONAT (see the equates). The CP/M builds always send ANSI.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In every build Ctrl-C stops a running program (an unchecked build stops
0000                             ;  without a word): see the console layer for the rules, the held key and
0000                             ;  the break-off cell.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80 (https://maly.github.io/asm80-node/), Z80 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   0   ; 1 = CP/M .COM build
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                EDITOR:   EQU   1   ; 1 = with the line editor
0000                ANSI:     EQU   1   ; 1 = the console escapes send ANSI sequences
0000                ANS:      EQU   ANSI+CPM-ANSI*CPM   ; (CP/M: always ANSI)
0000                PRSUB:    EQU   CHECKED   ; (1: "$" is the routine prstr)
0000                EDGEN:    EQU   EDITOR*(1-CPM)   ; (the generic build with the editor)
0000                             ; (IF takes any value but 0 as true, so
0000                             ;  IF CHECKED+EDITOR means "either")
0000                TABP0:    EQU   EDGEN*(1-CHECKED)   ; (the build with its table in page zero)
0000                PTLATE:   EQU   1-CPM*EDITOR*(1-CHECKED)   ; (1: the table goes after psgn and pdec,
0000                             ;   not before them: wherever it doesn't cross a
0000                             ;   page. chktab.py says if it does)
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    BC   IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    HL   TOS: the top data-stack cell is kept here, not in memory
0000                             ;    SP   the data stack: (SP) is NOS, the cell under TOS. The data stack is
0000                             ;         the Z80"s own stack, which is what the spec"s machine-code contract
0000                             ;         needs ("the data cells above the return address").
0000                             ;    HL'  return-stack pointer (the alternate HL). Entries are 2 bytes; the
0000                             ;         stack grows down. Only rpop and rpushn (and the checks) touch it.
0000                             ;    A DE scratch. Every handler is entered with HL = TOS and may use A, DE.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One-byte calls. The routines used most are reached with RST, one byte
0000                             ;  instead of three:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RST 08h  rpop    pop the return stack into DE
0000                             ;    RST 18h  drop    drop TOS, then next character     (ends a handler)
0000                             ;    RST 20h  neg16   HL = -HL
0000                             ;    RST 28h  putc    print A
0000                             ;    RST 30h  next    next character                    (ends a handler)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  RST 18h and RST 30h never return: an RST is a CALL, so the first thing
0000                             ;  each of them does is POP DE to throw the return address away.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The CP/M build can't own page zero, so the block from `vecs` to `vecend`
0000                             ;  (image addresses 0108h-0133h) is copied to 0008h-0033h when it starts. The
0000                             ;  code in that block is written to work at either place.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch. PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of
0000                             ;  its handler's address. The high byte is worked out from the character:
0000                             ;  the handlers of the first NPG1 characters (in code order) start in the
0000                             ;  image's second page, the rest in its first. The layout below keeps to
0000                             ;  that, and testing/chktab.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM pages:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RSPAGE   return stack, 112 entries (the pointer stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    DSPAGE   data stack, 127 cells (the top four bytes of the page are spare,
0000                             ;             so a full stack runs two bytes into the page below)
0000                             ;    LETPAGE  letter cells: A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h (so a word
0000                             ;             cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the heap pointer at
0000                             ;             +7Ch, interpreter variables in the gaps, and the -n? line buffer
0000                             ;             at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    PROG     the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts after the NUL
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range from the letter
0000                             ;  page up to the heap limit. Each stack has a guard band: the data stack can
0000                             ;  overrun by a cell or two (and the calls made while it is full, the error
0000                             ;  report's included) into the top 32 bytes of the return-stack page, which
0000                             ;  are never used, and the return stack by one entry into the page below it.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                          IF   CPM   
                    BDOS:     EQU   0005h   
                    BASE:     EQU   0100h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   CPM*(1-EDITOR)   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0000h   ; warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
0000                             ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The zero flag must match A
0000                             ;   (end the routine with OR A / RET).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                             ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve BC, DE, HL and HL'.
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   1-ANS   
                                 ; With ANSI = 0 the console escapes call these. All four must keep BC and
                                 ; HL'; CONCLS, CONEOL and CONCUR also DE and HL.
                    CONCLS:   EQU   0FF0Ch   ; /{  clear the screen, the cursor to the top left
                    CONEOL:   EQU   0FF0Fh   ; /}  clear from the cursor to the end of the line
                    CONCUR:   EQU   0FF12h   ; /| and /`  show the cursor if A is not 0, hide
                                 ;     it if A = 0
                    CONAT:    EQU   0FF15h   ; /~  the cursor to row HL, column DE, both
                                 ;     counted from 0. May change A, DE and HL
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
0000                RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   ; 8000h return stack
0000                DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   ; 8100h data stack
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   ; 8200h letter cells and line buffer
0000                PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
0000                BASE:     EQU   0000h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDGEN   
0000                LEAVE:    EQU   0FF09h   ; where the editor's ^X goes
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
                    LEAVE:    EQU   0000h   ; the editor's ^X: warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR   
0000                EXIT:     EQU   edend   ; a program that ends goes back to the editor,
0000                SKEND:    EQU   skend   ;   also when it ends inside skip
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   1-EDITOR   
                    SKEND:    EQU   EXIT   
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms (1-255):
0000                             ; each pass calls getk once, so tune it for
0000                             ; your clock and your KEY routine. (The wait
0000                             ; for a second Ctrl-C uses it too: 250 ms.)
0000                             ; letter-page layout (offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer
0000                RSAVE:    EQU   LET+34h   ; gap after Z: return stack pointer, saved
0000                             ;   around machine code (and in the checked
0000                             ;   build the address "$" prints from);
0000                NPEND:    EQU   LET+38h   ;   minus the address of the program's end
0000                             ;   (the heap"s first byte), for the checked "_';
0000                EDLN:     EQU   LET+3Ah   ;   the editor: the number of the line that ^E
0000                             ;   put in the input line (0: none)
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+7Ah   ; gap after z: a key read by the break check and
0000                             ;   held for the next "?" (0: none);
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   LET+7Bh   ;   the break-off cell: a program that stores a
0000                             ;   non-zero byte here gets Ctrl-C as a key
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+0E0h   ; empty return stack: the 32 bytes above it
0000                             ; take calls made while the data stack is full
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+0FCh   ; empty data stack. The four bytes above it
0000                             ; are spare: a character can pop two cells
0000                             ; too many before the checked build sees it,
0000                             ; and the next call must not land on the
0000                             ; letter cells.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  The first 49 bytes: the entry, then the RST routines, with small handlers
0000                             ;  and routines filling the gaps between them. Generic: this IS page zero.
0000                             ;  CP/M: it is the start of the .COM file, and 0108h-0133h is also copied to
0000                             ;  page zero (see the header).
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                          .ORG   BASE   
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              XOR   A   ; 00  reset. (This byte, AFh, is also what an
0000                          ENDIF      ;     undefined word runs into: see e_hi.)
0000                          IF   1-EDGEN   
                              LD   SP,DSTOP   ; 00  reset, or the start of the .COM file
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CHECKED)   
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; 03  the IP
                              JR   st0   ; 06  (the rest of the startup is close by)
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              JR   init   ; 04  (the rest of the startup is close by)
                              DW   0   ; 06  spare
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDGEN   
0000   AF                     XOR   A   ; 00  reset: no program yet. (This byte, AFh,
0001   32 00 83               LD   (PROG),A   ;     is also what an undefined word runs
0004   C3 E2 04               JP   init   ; 04  into in the checked build: see e_hi.)
0007   00                     NOP      ; 07  spare
0008                          ENDIF      
0008                          IF   CPM   
                              JP   start   ; 03
                              DW   0   ; 06  spare
0008                          ENDIF      
0008                VECS:        
0008                             ; ---- RST 08h: rpop: pop the return stack into DE ---------------------------
0008   D9           RPOP:     EXX      ; 08
0009   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
000A   23                     INC   HL   
000B   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
000C   23                     INC   HL   
000D   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; across to the main registers
000E   D9                     EXX      
000F   D1                     POP   DE   
0010   C9                     RET      ; 10  (so RST 10h is not used)
0011                             ; ctl: the inner loop comes here for characters below 21h. A = c - 21h.
0011   C6 21        CTL:      ADD   A,21h   ; 11  back to c; zero only for NUL
0013   20 1C                  JR   NZ,next0   ;     the rest are ignored
0015   C3 27 05     ENDPROG:   JP   EXIT   ;     the program has ended
0018                             ; ---- RST 18h: drop TOS, then next ------------------------------------------
0018   D1           RST18:    POP   DE   ; 18  discard the RST's return address
0019   E1                     POP   HL   ;     new TOS = NOS
001A   18 15                  JR   nx   
001C   E5           H_FROMR:   PUSH   HL   ; 1C  "}" return stack to TOS
001D   CF                     RST   08h   
001E   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
001F   F7                     RST   30h   
0020                             ; ---- RST 20h: neg16: HL = -HL (keeps BC, DE) -------------------------------
0020   AF           NEG16:    XOR   A   ; 20
0021   95                     SUB   L   
0022   6F                     LD   L,A   
0023   9F                     SBC   A,A   
0024   94                     SUB   H   
0025   67                     LD   H,A   
0026   C9                     RET      
0027   00                     NOP      ; 27  spare
0028                             ; ---- RST 28h: putc: print A (keeps BC, DE, HL, HL') ------------------------
0028                RST28:       
0028                          IFN   CPM   
0028   C3 03 FF     PUTC:     JP   CONOUT   ; 28
002B                          ENDIF      
002B                          IF   CPM   
                              JP   putc   ; 28
002B                          ENDIF      
002B   E9           JPHL:     JP   (HL)   ; 2B  (for the machine-code call)
002C   E3           H_TOR:    EX   (SP),HL   ; 2C  "{" TOS to the return stack: the new TOS
002D   C3 B7 00               JP   rpushn   ;     comes up, the old one goes across
0030                             ; ---- RST 30h: next character -----------------------------------------------
0030   D1           RST30:    POP   DE   ; 30  discard the RST's return address
0031                NX:          
0031                          IF   CPM   
                              JP   next0   ; (this copy runs in page zero)
0031                          ENDIF      
0031                VECEND:      
0031                             ; =============================================================================
0031                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
0031                             ; 
0031                             ;    00h          end of program
0031                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
0031                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
0031                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
0031                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
0031                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
0031                             ; =============================================================================
0031                NEXT0:       
0031                          IF   CHECKED   
0031   CD BB 03               CALL   chkstk   ; both stacks are checked once per character
0034                          ENDIF      
0034   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
0035   03                     INC   BC   
0036   D6 21                  SUB   21h   ; A = c - 21h
0038   38 D7                  JR   C,ctl   ; c < 21h: NUL ends, the rest are ignored
003A   FE 0F                  CP   0Fh   
003C   38 25                  JR   C,punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
003E   D6 0F                  SUB   0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
0040   FE 0A                  CP   0Ah   
0042   38 5D                  JR   C,digit   ; 30h-39h
0044   FE 11                  CP   11h   
0046   38 19                  JR   C,p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
0048   D6 11                  SUB   11h   ; A = c - 41h
004A   FE 1A                  CP   1Ah   
004C   38 5F                  JR   C,upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
004E   FE 20                  CP   20h   
0050   38 0D                  JR   C,p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
0052   FE 3A                  CP   3Ah   
0054   38 51                  JR   C,lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
0056   FE 3E                  CP   3Eh   
0058                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              JR   NC,next0   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
0058                          ENDIF      
0058                          IF   CHECKED   
0058   28 D7                  JR   Z,next0   ; 7Fh, DEL: ignored
005A   D2 E7 03               JP   NC,e_hi   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
005D                          ENDIF      
005D   D6 1A                  SUB   1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
005F   D6 09        P5B:      SUB   9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
0061   C6 05        P3A:      ADD   A,5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
0063                .macro PTABLE,
0063                             ; 
0063                 DB      h_store & 0FFh  ; !
0063                 DB      h_str & 0FFh    ; "
0063                 DB      h_num & 0FFh    ; #
0063                 DB      h_print & 0FFh  ; $
0063                 DB      h_swap & 0FFh   ; %
0063                 DB      h_and & 0FFh    ; &
0063                 DB      h_emit & 0FFh   ; '
0063                 DB      h_open & 0FFh   ; (
0063                 DB      h_close & 0FFh  ; )
0063                 DB      h_mul & 0FFh    ; *
0063                 DB      h_add & 0FFh    ; +
0063                 DB      h_cfetch & 0FFh ; ,
0063                 DB      h_sub & 0FFh    ; -
0063                 DB      h_cstore & 0FFh ; .
0063                 DB      h_div & 0FFh    ; /
0063                 DB      h_dup & 0FFh    ; :
0063                 DB      h_drop & 0FFh   ; ;
0063                 DB      h_lt & 0FFh     ; <
0063                 DB      h_eq & 0FFh     ; =
0063                 DB      h_gt & 0FFh     ; >
0063                 DB      h_key & 0FFh    ; ?
0063                 DB      h_fetch & 0FFh  ; @
0063                 DB      h_def & 0FFh    ; [
0063                 DB      h_break & 0FFh  ; \
0063                 DB      h_ret & 0FFh    ; ]
0063                 DB      h_xor & 0FFh    ; ^
0063                 DB      h_alloc & 0FFh  ; _
0063                 DB      h_grave & 0FFh  ; `
0063                 DB      h_tor & 0FFh    ; {
0063                 DB      h_or & 0FFh     ; |
0063                 DB      h_fromr & 0FFh  ; }
0063                 DB      h_not & 0FFh    ; ~
0063                .endm
0063                 
0063                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index. The handler starts with HL = TOS,
0063                             ; untouched, and A, DE free.
0063   C6 5D        PUNCT:    ADD   A,PTAB & 0FFh   ; PTAB never crosses a page
0065   5F                     LD   E,A   
0066   16 03                  LD   D,PTAB / 256   ; (0 if the table is in page zero)
0068   FE 73                  CP   (PTAB & 0FFh) + NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
006A   1A                     LD   A,(DE)   
006B   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the handler's low byte
006C                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-TABP0)   
006C   16 00                  LD   D,0   
006E                          ENDIF      
006E                          IFN   CPM   
006E   CB 12                  RL   D   ; its page: 0 + carry
0070                          ENDIF      
0070                          IF   CPM   
                              LD   D,1   
                              JR   NC,pu1   
                              INC   D   ; its page: 1 + carry
                    PU1:         
0070                          ENDIF      
0070   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; jump to it; the stack is balanced again
0071   C9                     RET      ;   when the handler starts
0072                             ; The rest of the startup: here so that the generic reset code can reach it
0072                             ; with JR. st0: find the program's NUL; the heap starts after it.
0072                             ; (The editor build has its own copy of this, next to the editor.)
0072                             ; A checked build first clears the lower half of the letter page (A = 0):
0072                             ; every variable starts at 0, every word cell holds 0000h, the address an
0072                             ; undefined word is caught at (see e_hi), and no key is held back.
0072                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                    INIT:     LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; the IP
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    ST0:      LD   H,B   
                              LD   L,C   
                              XOR   A   
                    ST1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,st1   
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   1-EDITOR   
                    ST2:      LD   (HEAP),HL   
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
                              RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
                              LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CPM)   
                              LD   H,A   ; (A = 0) no key is held, and the break key
                              LD   L,A   ;   is on (the checked build has cleared
0072                          ENDIF      ;   these)
0072                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)*CPM   
                              LD   HL,0   
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                              LD   (KEYBUF),HL   
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                          IF   1-EDITOR   
                              EXX      
                              LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
                              EXX      
                              RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                             ; In the unchecked generic editor build the table is here, in the first
0072                             ; page, which saves loading D twice. (The other builds have no room for it
0072                             ; here: theirs is further down.)
0072                          IF   TABP0   
                    PTAB:        
                              ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
                              DB   h_store & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_str & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_num & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_print & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_and & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_open & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_close & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_add & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_div & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_key & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_def & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_break & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_or & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_not & 0FFh   
                    PTABEND:      
0072                          ENDIF      
0072                             ; =============================================================================
0072                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's first page: ^ _ ` | ~
0072                             ;  (00bbIGFuZCA= are up among the RST routines.) The machine-code call, exec,
0072                             ;  is here too: it belongs to "`" and makes the page come out right.
0072                             ; =============================================================================
0072   D1           H_XOR:    POP   DE   
0073   7C                     LD   A,H   
0074   AA                     XOR   D   
0075   67                     LD   H,A   
0076   7D                     LD   A,L   
0077   AB                     XOR   E   
0078   6F                     LD   L,A   
0079   F7                     RST   30h   
007A   D1           H_OR:     POP   DE   
007B   7C                     LD   A,H   
007C   B2                     OR   D   
007D   67                     LD   H,A   
007E   7D                     LD   A,L   
007F   B3                     OR   E   
0080   6F                     LD   L,A   
0081   F7                     RST   30h   
0082   E7           H_NOT:    RST   20h   ; ~x = -x - 1
0083   2B                     DEC   HL   
0084   F7                     RST   30h   
0085                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n, a signed count (the add is
0085                             ; the same either way); TOS is the old pointer.
0085   ED 5B 7C 82  H_ALLOC:   LD   DE,(HEAP)   
0089                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              LD   A,H   ; the count's sign, for chkhp
0089                          ENDIF      
0089   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; the new top
008A                          IF   CHECKED   
008A   CD F1 03               CALL   chkhp   
008D                          ENDIF      
008D   22 7C 82               LD   (HEAP),HL   
0090   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0091   F7                     RST   30h   
0092   D9           EXEC:     EXX      
0093   22 34 82               LD   (RSAVE),HL   ; machine code may change the alternates
0096   D9                     EXX      
0097   CD 2B 00               CALL   jphl   
009A   D9                     EXX      
009B   2A 34 82               LD   HL,(RSAVE)   
009E   D9                     EXX      
009F   E1                     POP   HL   
00A0   F7                     RST   30h   
00A1                             ; ---- the letters and digits (here, in the middle, so that the inner loop's
00A1                             ; ---- short jumps reach them, and the handlers after them reach rpushn) ------
00A1                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
00A1   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   HL   
00A2   0B                     DEC   BC   
00A3   CD CD 02               CALL   rdnum   
00A6   F7                     RST   30h   
00A7                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
00A7   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   HL   
00A8   87                     ADD   A,A   
00A9   6F                     LD   L,A   
00AA   26 82                  LD   H,LETPAGE   
00AC   F7                     RST   30h   
00AD                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
00AD                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
00AD   C5           UPPER:    PUSH   BC   ; the return address, for rpushn
00AE   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; park TOS
00AF   87                     ADD   A,A   
00B0   6F                     LD   L,A   
00B1   26 82                  LD   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
00B3   4E                     LD   C,(HL)   
00B4   2C                     INC   L   
00B5   46                     LD   B,(HL)   ; IP = the word's body
00B6   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; TOS back, and fall into rpushn
00B7                             ; rpushn: move the top cell of the data stack (in memory) to the return
00B7                             ; stack, then next. Everything that pushes the return stack ends here.
00B7                             ; 
00B7                             ; The break key is looked at here, so at every word call and loop-back (and
00B7                             ; block entry and "{"), but only one time in 256: B', which nothing else
00B7                             ; uses, counts them. Reading the keyboard can be slow (it is a BDOS call
00B7                             ; under CP/M), and this way it costs a loop four bytes and 14 T-states.
00B7                             ; (DEC B, not DJNZ: its zero flag lasts through the EXX, so one EXX serves
00B7                             ; both ways out.)
00B7   D9           RPUSHN:   EXX      
00B8   D1                     POP   DE   
00B9   2B                     DEC   HL   
00BA   72                     LD   (HL),D   
00BB   2B                     DEC   HL   
00BC   73                     LD   (HL),E   
00BD   05                     DEC   B   
00BE   D9                     EXX      
00BF   CC 7D 03               CALL   Z,pollk   
00C2   F7                     RST   30h   
00C3                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
00C3                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
00C3                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (C9h) is
00C3                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
00C3                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
00C3                             ; code is entered by CALL with the data stack above the return address; it
00C3                             ; must keep BC, and on return the top cell becomes the new TOS.
00C3   CD 31 03     H_GRAVE:   CALL   hexc   
00C6   30 CA                  JR   NC,exec   
00C8   77           HX1:      LD   (HL),A   ; the high digit goes in first ...
00C9   CD 31 03               CALL   hexc   
00CC   30 08                  JR   NC,hx2   ; odd digit: consumed, and the RET below
00CE   ED 6F                  RLD      ;   overwrites it
00D0   23                     INC   HL   ; ... and RLD shifts it up under the low one
00D1   CD 31 03               CALL   hexc   
00D4   38 F2                  JR   C,hx1   
00D6   36 C9        HX2:      LD   (HL),0C9h   ; (never range-checked: the spec says so)
00D8   F7                     RST   30h   
00D9                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
00D9                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
00D9                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
00D9                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
00D9                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
00D9                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it.
00D9   CF           H_RET:    RST   08h   
00DA   42                     LD   B,D   
00DB   4B                     LD   C,E   
00DC   F7           BRK1:     RST   30h   
00DD                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
00DD                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
00DD   7C           H_BREAK:   LD   A,H   
00DE   B5                     OR   L   
00DF   E1                     POP   HL   
00E0   28 FA                  JR   Z,brk1   
00E2   CD F4 02               CALL   skip   
00E5   B7                     OR   A   ; skip returns 0 for ")"
00E6   20 F1                  JR   NZ,h_ret   
00E8   CF           RDROP:    RST   08h   
00E9   F7                     RST   30h   
00EA                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
00EA                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
00EA                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
00EA                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
00EA                             ; checked build stops on it.)
00EA   0A           H_DEF:    LD   A,(BC)   
00EB   03                     INC   BC   
00EC   D6 41                  SUB   "A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
00EE   5F                     LD   E,A   ;   lands 64 bytes up
00EF   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   ; fold case
00F1   FE 1A                  CP   26   
00F3   30 0B                  JR   NC,def2   ; not a letter
00F5   CB 23                  SLA   E   
00F7   16 82                  LD   D,LETPAGE   ; DE -> cell
00F9   79                     LD   A,C   
00FA   12                     LD   (DE),A   
00FB   1C                     INC   E   
00FC   78                     LD   A,B   
00FD   12                     LD   (DE),A   
00FE   18 09                  JR   skipnx   
0100                DEF2:        
0100                          IF   CHECKED   
0100   7B                     LD   A,E   
0101   FE DF                  CP   " "-"A"+256   
0103   C2 23 04               JP   NZ,e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
0106                          ENDIF      
0106   E5                     PUSH   HL   ; an anonymous block: push its address
0107   60                     LD   H,B   
0108   69                     LD   L,C   
0109                SKIPNX:      
0109                          IF   CHECKED   
0109   0B                     DEC   BC   ; back onto the letter, so that skip finds its
010A                          ENDIF      ;   opener, the "[", just before where it starts
010A   CD F4 02     SKIPO:    CALL   skip   
010D   F7                     RST   30h   
010E   5E           H_FETCH:   LD   E,(HL)   ; "@"
010F   23                     INC   HL   
0110   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
0111   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0112   F7                     RST   30h   
0113                             ; =============================================================================
0113                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's second page.
0113                             ;  "?" is the last (with "," inside it), so its long tail may run past that
0113                             ;  page.
0113                             ; =============================================================================
0113                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
0113                             ; the matching ")".
0113   7C           H_OPEN:   LD   A,H   
0114   B5                     OR   L   
0115   E1                     POP   HL   
0116   28 F2                  JR   Z,skipo   
0118   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; the block starts at the IP
0119   18 9C                  JR   rpushn   
011B                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
011B                             ; drops it and carries on.
011B   7C           H_CLOSE:   LD   A,H   
011C   B5                     OR   L   
011D   E1                     POP   HL   
011E   28 C8                  JR   Z,rdrop   
0120   CF                     RST   08h   ; pop the block start ...
0121   42                     LD   B,D   
0122   4B                     LD   C,E   
0123   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0124   18 91                  JR   rpushn   ; ... and push it back
0126                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
0126                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
0126   0A           H_SUB:    LD   A,(BC)   
0127   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
0129   FE 0A                  CP   10   
012B   38 04                  JR   C,negnum   
012D   E7                     RST   20h   ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into "+"
012E   D1           H_ADD:    POP   DE   
012F   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0130   F7                     RST   30h   
0131   E5           NEGNUM:   PUSH   HL   ; a negative number: read it, negate it
0132   CD CD 02               CALL   rdnum   
0135   E7                     RST   20h   
0136   F7                     RST   30h   
0137   D1           H_AND:    POP   DE   
0138   7C                     LD   A,H   
0139   A2                     AND   D   
013A   67                     LD   H,A   
013B   7D                     LD   A,L   
013C   A3                     AND   E   
013D   6F                     LD   L,A   
013E   F7                     RST   30h   
013F                             ; Signed compares. Both are "HL < DE" for the right pair: "<" swaps the two
013F                             ; cells first. Flipping both sign bits turns a signed compare into an
013F                             ; unsigned one (and XOR clears the carry for SBC); SBC HL,HL then turns the
013F                             ; carry into -1 or 0 with no branch.
013F   E3           H_LT:     EX   (SP),HL   ; a < b: HL = a, and b is popped next
0140   D1           H_GT:     POP   DE   ; a > b  is  b < a: HL = b, DE = a
0141   7C                     LD   A,H   
0142   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
0144   67                     LD   H,A   
0145   7A                     LD   A,D   
0146   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
0148   57                     LD   D,A   
0149   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry if HL < DE
014B   ED 62        TF:       SBC   HL,HL   ; carry -> -1 or 0
014D   F7                     RST   30h   
014E   D1           H_EQ:     POP   DE   
014F   B7                     OR   A   
0150   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
0152   7C                     LD   A,H   
0153   B5                     OR   L   
0154   FE 01                  CP   1   ; carry only if a - b = 0
0156   18 F3                  JR   tf   
0158                             ; "*": shift-and-add, 16 rounds; only the low 16 bits are kept. The
0158                             ; multiplier shifts up through A:C.
0158   D1           H_MUL:    POP   DE   ; DE = multiplicand
0159   C5                     PUSH   BC   
015A   7C                     LD   A,H   
015B   4D                     LD   C,L   ; A:C = multiplier
015C   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
015F   06 10                  LD   B,16   
0161   29           MUL1:     ADD   HL,HL   
0162   CB 21                  SLA   C   
0164   17                     RLA      
0165   30 01                  JR   NC,mul2   
0167   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0168   10 F7        MUL2:     DJNZ   mul1   
016A   C1                     POP   BC   
016B   F7                     RST   30h   
016C                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
016C                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
016C                             ; of a. Dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; the checked build
016C                             ; stops on it.
016C                H_DIV:       
016C                          IF   CHECKED   
016C   7C                     LD   A,H   
016D   B5                     OR   L   
016E   CA 20 04               JP   Z,e_zero   
0171                          ENDIF      
0171   D1                     POP   DE   ; DE = a, HL = b
0172   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; a, for r's sign
0173   7A                     LD   A,D   
0174   AC                     XOR   H   
0175   F5                     PUSH   AF   ; S flag = sign of q
0176   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
0178   C4 20 00               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |b|
017B   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
017C   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
017E   C4 20 00               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |a|, DE = |b|
0181   CD A5 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = q, DE = r
0184   F1                     POP   AF   
0185   FC 20 00               CALL   M,neg16   ; q's sign
0188   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; HL = r, DE = q
0189   F1                     POP   AF   ; A = a's high byte
018A   B7                     OR   A   
018B   FC 20 00               CALL   M,neg16   ; r's sign
018E   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; q under r
018F   F7                     RST   30h   
0190                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
0190   E5           H_DUP:    PUSH   HL   ; ":"
0191   F7                     RST   30h   
0192   E3           H_SWAP:   EX   (SP),HL   ; "%"
0193   F7                     RST   30h   
0194                             ; (The checked build tests the address before it takes the value off the
0194                             ; stack, so that an error report shows both.)
0194                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
0194                          IF   CHECKED   
0194   CD 06 04               CALL   chkst   
0197                          ENDIF      
0197   D1                     POP   DE   
0198   73                     LD   (HL),E   
0199   DF           H_DROP:   RST   18h   ; ";" is this one byte
019A                H_STORE:      ; "!" ( n addr -- )
019A                          IF   CHECKED   
019A   CD 06 04               CALL   chkst   
019D                          ENDIF      
019D   D1                     POP   DE   
019E   73                     LD   (HL),E   
019F   23                     INC   HL   
01A0   72                     LD   (HL),D   
01A1   DF                     RST   18h   
01A2                             ; ---- console ---------------------------------------------------------------
01A2                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
01A2   E5           H_STR:    PUSH   HL   
01A3   60                     LD   H,B   
01A4   69                     LD   L,C   
01A5   CD E3 02               CALL   skipstr   
01A8                          IF   CHECKED   
01A8   B7                     OR   A   ; 0: the text ran out before the closing quote
01A9   CA 18 04               JP   Z,e_quote   
01AC                          ENDIF      
01AC   F7                     RST   30h   
01AD                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character from
01AD                             ; 60h to 7Eh is one of the escapes at pesc; "/" plus any other character
01AD                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /? is DEL"s "?"; "/" and """ have
01AD                             ; no bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
01AD                          IF   1-PRSUB   
                    H_PRINT:   LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   22h   
                              JR   Z,pr9   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   NZ,pr1   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   60h   
                              JR   C,pr0   
                              CP   7Fh   
                              JR   C,pesc   
                    PR0:      AND   0BFh   
                    PR1:      RST   28h   
                              JR   h_print   
                    PRLOOP:   EQU   h_print   ; (where the escapes go back to)
                    PRAGAIN:   EQU   h_print   ; (and where /~ goes back to)
01AD                          ENDIF      
01AD                          IF   CHECKED   
01AD                             ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the error
01AD                             ; report uses too. The address is kept meanwhile, for a report: it shows
01AD                             ; the stack as it was before the "$". /~ comes back to hp1.)
01AD   22 34 82     H_PRINT:   LD   (RSAVE),HL   
01B0   CD 06 02     HP1:      CALL   prstr   
01B3   DF                     RST   18h   
01B4                          ENDIF      
01B4   7D           H_EMIT:   LD   A,L   ; "'"
01B5   EF                     RST   28h   
01B6   DF           PR9:      RST   18h   
01B7                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
01B7   CD 43 03     H_NUM:    CALL   psgn   
01BA   DF                     RST   18h   
01BB                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
01BB                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
01BB                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
01BB                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
01BB                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
01BB   CB 7C        H_KEY:    BIT   7,H   
01BD   20 19                  JR   NZ,line   
01BF   1E 28        KT1:      LD   E,MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
01C1   CD AB 03     KT2:      CALL   getk   
01C4   20 0E                  JR   NZ,kt3   
01C6   1D                     DEC   E   
01C7   20 F8                  JR   NZ,kt2   
01C9   7C                     LD   A,H   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
01CA   B5                     OR   L   
01CB   28 F2                  JR   Z,kt1   
01CD   2B                     DEC   HL   
01CE   7C                     LD   A,H   
01CF   B5                     OR   L   
01D0   20 ED                  JR   NZ,kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
01D2   FE                     DB   0FEh   ; (CP n: steps over the one byte of ",")
01D3   7E           H_CFETCH:   LD   A,(HL)   ; "," shares "?"s ending: A becomes TOS
01D4   6F           KT3:      LD   L,A   
01D5   26 00                  LD   H,0   
01D7   F7                     RST   30h   
01D8                             ; Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as
01D8                             ; it is), CR ends (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and
01D8                             ; echoed until the line is full. The line buffer starts at offset 80h
01D8                             ; of its page, so L alone is the place in the line: D holds the L of
01D8                             ; a full line.
01D8   11 7F 00     LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
01DB   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
01DC   9F                     SBC   A,A   
01DD   A5                     AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
01DE   2F                     CPL      
01DF   57                     LD   D,A   ; D = the L of a full line: 80h + count, FFh
01E0                             ;   at most
01E0   21 80 82               LD   HL,LINEBUF   
01E3   CD AB 03     LN2:      CALL   getk   
01E6   28 FB                  JR   Z,ln2   
01E8   FE 0D                  CP   13   
01EA   28 16                  JR   Z,ln5   
01EC   FE 08                  CP   8   
01EE   28 0B                  JR   Z,ln4   
01F0   5F                     LD   E,A   
01F1   7D                     LD   A,L   
01F2   BA                     CP   D   
01F3   28 EE                  JR   Z,ln2   ; full
01F5   73                     LD   (HL),E   
01F6   2C                     INC   L   
01F7   7B                     LD   A,E   
01F8   EF           LN3:      RST   28h   
01F9   18 E8                  JR   ln2   
01FB   2D           LN4:      DEC   L   ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
01FC   FA F8 01               JP   M,ln3   ;   unless the line was empty (L left the
01FF   2C                     INC   L   ;   upper half of the page)
0200   18 E1                  JR   ln2   
0202   77           LN5:      LD   (HL),A   ; the CR
0203   2E 80                  LD   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
0205   F7                     RST   30h   
0206                             ; =============================================================================
0206                             ;  More routines (no handler starts past this point)
0206                             ; =============================================================================
0206                          IF   CHECKED   
0206                             ; prstr: print the string at HL, to its closing quote, decoding "/" (this is
0206                             ; "$", and the texts of the report). A NUL first is an error: Q.
0206   7E           PRSTR:    LD   A,(HL)   
0207   23                     INC   HL   
0208   FE 22                  CP   22h   
020A   C8                     RET   Z   
020B   B7                     OR   A   
020C   28 1F                  JR   Z,e_dollar   
020E   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
0210   20 0C                  JR   NZ,prs1   
0212   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0213   23                     INC   HL   
0214   FE 60                  CP   60h   
0216   38 04                  JR   C,prs0   
0218   FE 7F                  CP   7Fh   
021A   38 1A                  JR   C,pesc   
021C   E6 BF        PRS0:     AND   0BFh   
021E   EF           PRS1:     RST   28h   
021F   18 E5                  JR   prstr   
0221                PRLOOP:   EQU   prstr   ; (where the escapes go back to)
0221                PRAGAIN:   EQU   hp1   ; (and where /~ goes back to)
0221                             ; pmsg: print the text that follows the CALL, to its closing quote. Keeps HL.
0221                             ; pnl: the same, on a new line.
0221   3E 0D        PNL:      LD   A,13   
0223   EF                     RST   28h   
0224   3E 0A                  LD   A,10   
0226   EF                     RST   28h   
0227   E3           PMSG:     EX   (SP),HL   
0228   CD 06 02               CALL   prstr   
022B   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   
022C   C9                     RET      
022D   D1           E_DOLLAR:   POP   DE   ; "$" ran into a NUL: drop the return address,
022E   2A 34 82               LD   HL,(RSAVE)   ;   and put the string's address back in TOS
0231   3E 51                  LD   A,"Q"   
0233   C3 25 04               JP   error   
0236                          ENDIF      
0236                             ; pesc: the escapes of "$". A = the character after the "/", 60h to 7Eh, and
0236                             ; HL points past it. Each goes back into the loop that prints the string
0236                             ; (PRLOOP), but /~ has the stack to see to, and goes back by PRAGAIN.
0236                             ;    /a-/z   print the variable, as "#" does
0236                             ;    /{      clear the screen, the cursor to the top left
0236                             ;    /}      clear from the cursor to the end of the line
0236                             ;    /|  /`  show the cursor, hide it
0236                             ;    /~      ( row col -- ) the cursor to that row and column, from 0
0236   FE 7E        PESC:     CP   7Eh   
0238   28 1C                  JR   Z,pat   
023A   11 06 02               LD   DE,PRLOOP   ; the others return into the loop
023D   D5                     PUSH   DE   
023E   D6 7B                  SUB   7Bh   ; 00bbIDAsIHwgMSwg 2, and no borrow
0240   30 31                  JR   NC,pcon   
0242   C6 1A                  ADD   A,1Ah   ; a-z: 0-25, and a carry; `: FFh, and none
0244   30 41                  JR   NC,phide   
0246   87                     ADD   A,A   ; the variable's cell
0247   C6 40                  ADD   A,40h   
0249   E5                     PUSH   HL   
024A   6F                     LD   L,A   
024B   26 82                  LD   H,LETPAGE   
024D   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
024E   2C                     INC   L   
024F   66                     LD   H,(HL)   
0250   6F                     LD   L,A   
0251   CD 43 03               CALL   psgn   
0254   E1                     POP   HL   
0255   C9                     RET      
0256                             ; /~ ( row col addr -- ): the two cells under the string's address go. Where
0256                             ; "$" is the routine prstr, its own return address goes first, and hp1
0256                             ; calls it again afterwards. (The checked build looks first, through
0256                             ; chkstk, that there is a column at least: with less, it is s. With a
0256                             ; column but no row it is s after the "$", as for any other character; the
0256                             ; spare bytes above the stack take what is written meanwhile.)
0256                PAT:         
0256                          IF   PRSUB   
0256   D1                     POP   DE   
0257                          ENDIF      
0257                          IF   CHECKED   
0257   CD BB 03               CALL   chkstk   
025A                          ENDIF      
025A   D1                     POP   DE   ; DE = the column
025B   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   ; HL = the row; the text pointer is kept
025C                          IF   1-ANS   
                              CALL   CONAT   
                              POP   HL   
                              JP   PRAGAIN   
                                 ; With ANSI = 0 the machine's routines do the rest.
                    PHIDE:    XOR   A   ; /`  (A = 0: hide)
                              JP   CONCUR   
                    PCON:     JP   Z,CONCLS   ; /{
                              CP   2   
                              JP   Z,CONEOL   ; /}
                              JP   CONCUR   ; /|  (A = 1: show)
025C                          ENDIF      
025C                          IF   ANS   
025C   D5                     PUSH   DE   
025D   CD 9C 02               CALL   csi   ; ESC [ row+1 ; col+1 H (ANSI counts from 1)
0260   23                     INC   HL   
0261   CD 4B 03               CALL   pdec   
0264   3E 3B                  LD   A,";"   
0266   EF                     RST   28h   
0267   E1                     POP   HL   
0268   23                     INC   HL   
0269   CD 4B 03               CALL   pdec   
026C   3E 48                  LD   A,"H"   
026E   EF                     RST   28h   
026F   E1                     POP   HL   
0270   C3 B0 01               JP   PRAGAIN   
0273                             ; With ANSI = 1 they are sequences. The carry is clear on the way in.
0273   3D           PCON:     DEC   A   
0274   28 0E                  JR   Z,pshow   ; /|
0276   3E 4B                  LD   A,"K"   
0278   F2 97 02               JP   P,csia   ; /}  ESC [ K
027B   3E 48                  LD   A,"H"   ; /{  ESC [ H ESC [ J
027D   CD 97 02               CALL   csia   
0280   3E 4A                  LD   A,"J"   
0282   18 13                  JR   csia   
0284   1E 68        PSHOW:    LD   E,"h"   ; /|  ESC [ ? 2 5 h
0286   DA                     DB   0DAh   ; (JP C,nn: with no carry it steps over two bytes)
0287   1E 6C        PHIDE:    LD   E,"l"   ; /`  ESC [ ? 2 5 l
0289   3E 3F                  LD   A,"?"   
028B   CD 97 02               CALL   csia   
028E   3E 32                  LD   A,"2"   
0290   EF                     RST   28h   
0291   3E 35                  LD   A,"5"   
0293   EF                     RST   28h   
0294   7B                     LD   A,E   
0295   EF                     RST   28h   
0296   C9                     RET      
0297                             ; csia: ESC [ and then A. csi: ESC [, keeping A.
0297   CD 9C 02     CSIA:     CALL   csi   
029A   EF                     RST   28h   
029B   C9                     RET      
029C   F5           CSI:      PUSH   AF   
029D   3E 1B                  LD   A,27   
029F   EF                     RST   28h   
02A0   3E 5B                  LD   A,"["   
02A2   EF                     RST   28h   
02A3   F1                     POP   AF   
02A4   C9                     RET      
02A5                          ENDIF      
02A5                             ; udiv: unsigned HL / DE (DE <= 8000h). Returns HL = quotient, DE = remainder.
02A5                             ; Uses A; keeps BC (the IP) itself. The dividend shifts up through A:C while
02A5                             ; the quotient bits arrive at the bottom of C.
02A5                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
02A5   7B           UDIV:     LD   A,E   
02A6   EE 02                  XOR   2   
02A8   B2                     OR   D   
02A9   20 07                  JR   NZ,udv0   
02AB   CB 3C                  SRL   H   
02AD   CB 1D                  RR   L   ; the quotient
02AF   8F                     ADC   A,A   
02B0   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out (D is 0)
02B1   C9                     RET      
02B2   C5           UDV0:     PUSH   BC   
02B3   7C                     LD   A,H   
02B4   4D                     LD   C,L   
02B5   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
02B8   06 10                  LD   B,16   
02BA   CB 21        UDV1:     SLA   C   
02BC   17                     RLA      
02BD   ED 6A                  ADC   HL,HL   
02BF   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry is clear here: the remainder
02C1   30 02                  JR   NC,udv2   ;   always fits in 16 bits
02C3   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; too much: put it back, and cancel the
02C4   0D                     DEC   C   ;   INC below
02C5   0C           UDV2:     INC   C   ; a quotient bit
02C6   10 F2                  DJNZ   udv1   
02C8   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; DE = remainder
02C9   67                     LD   H,A   
02CA   69                     LD   L,C   ; HL = quotient
02CB   C1                     POP   BC   
02CC   C9                     RET      
02CD                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP into HL; IP is left on the first
02CD                             ; non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says.
02CD   21 00 00     RDNUM:    LD   HL,0   
02D0   0A           RDN1:     LD   A,(BC)   
02D1   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
02D3   FE 0A                  CP   10   
02D5   D0                     RET   NC   
02D6   03                     INC   BC   
02D7   54                     LD   D,H   
02D8   5D                     LD   E,L   
02D9   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
02DA   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
02DB   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
02DC   29                     ADD   HL,HL   ; HL * 10
02DD   5F                     LD   E,A   
02DE   16 00                  LD   D,0   
02E0   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
02E1   18 ED                  JR   rdn1   
02E3                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
02E3                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h.
02E3                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    SS0:      INC   BC   
                    SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
                              INC   BC   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   Z,ss0   
                              CP   22h   
                              JR   NZ,skipstr   
                              RET      
02E3                          ENDIF      
02E3                          IF   CHECKED   
02E3                             ; The checked build never steps over a NUL: if the text runs out first it
02E3                             ; returns A = 0 with the IP on the NUL.
02E3   0A           SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
02E4   B7                     OR   A   
02E5   C8                     RET   Z   
02E6   03                     INC   BC   
02E7   FE 22                  CP   22h   
02E9   C8                     RET   Z   
02EA   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
02EC   20 F5                  JR   NZ,skipstr   
02EE   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   ; the escaped character
02EF   B7                     OR   A   
02F0   C8                     RET   Z   
02F1   03                     INC   BC   
02F2   18 EF                  JR   skipstr   
02F4                          ENDIF      
02F4                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
02F4                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
02F4                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
02F4                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
02F4                             ; anyway). D counts the open levels, starting at 1 for the one we are in:
02F4                             ; skip sets it to 0 and falls through the INC that an opener comes back to.
02F4                             ; 
02F4                             ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
02F4                             ; which is always the one just before where it starts: "(" must end at ")",
02F4                             ; "[" at "]", and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
02F4                             ; quote counts as running into it. "\" takes either closer. IX keeps the
02F4                             ; place where the skip started, for the report.
02F4                SKIP:        
02F4                          IF   CHECKED   
02F4   C5                     PUSH   BC   
02F5   DD E1                  POP   IX   
02F7   0B                     DEC   BC   
02F8   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
02F9   03                     INC   BC   
02FA   5F                     LD   E,A   ; E = the opener: ( [ or \
02FB                          ENDIF      
02FB   16 00                  LD   D,0   
02FD   14           SK3:      INC   D   ; an opener: one deeper
02FE   0A           SK1:      LD   A,(BC)   
02FF                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              INC   BC   
                              OR   A   
                              JP   Z,SKEND   ; (the end of the program)
02FF                          ENDIF      
02FF                          IF   CHECKED   
02FF   B7                     OR   A   
0300   28 22                  JR   Z,sk6   ; (the IP stays on the NUL)
0302   03                     INC   BC   
0303                          ENDIF      
0303   FE 22                  CP   22h   
0305   CC E3 02               CALL   Z,skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
0308   D6 28                  SUB   "("   ;   (or 0, and then the NUL is read next)
030A   28 F1                  JR   Z,sk3   
030C   3D                     DEC   A   ; ")"
030D   28 08                  JR   Z,sk4   
030F   D6 32                  SUB   "["-")"   
0311   28 EA                  JR   Z,sk3   
0313   FE 02                  CP   "]"-"["   
0315   20 E7                  JR   NZ,sk1   
0317   15           SK4:      DEC   D   
0318                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              RET   Z   ; the closer at this level
                              JR   sk1   
0318                          ENDIF      
0318                          IF   CHECKED   
0318   20 E4                  JR   NZ,sk1   
031A   57                     LD   D,A   ; the closer at this level: 0 or 2. Bit 1 of the
031B   AB                     XOR   E   ;   opener is 0 for "(" and 1 for "[", and only
031C   E6 06                  AND   6   ;   "\" has bit 2: so this is 2 for the wrong
031E   FE 02                  CP   2   ;   closer, and only then
0320   7A                     LD   A,D   
0321   C0                     RET   NZ   
0322   18 05                  JR   sk7   
0324   CB 53        SK6:      BIT   2,E   ; the text ran out:
0326   C2 26 05               JP   NZ,SKEND   ;   "\" with no closer ends the program
0329   DD E5        SK7:      PUSH   IX   ; N. The place is the opener
032B   C1                     POP   BC   
032C   3E 4E                  LD   A,"N"   
032E   C3 15 04               JP   errp   ; (errp drops skip's return address)
0331                          ENDIF      
0331                             ; =============================================================================
0331                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of each handler's address, in code order
0331                             ;  (the table itself is the macro PTABLE, defined above the dispatcher).
0331                             ;  It must not cross a page (the dispatcher only adds to its low byte).
0331                             ; =============================================================================
0331                             ; The handlers of the first NPG1 characters start in the image's second page.
0331                             ; ] \ [ @ sit where the two pages meet, and which side each lands on
0331                             ; differs between the builds, so the count is worked out here.
0331                             ; (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it stores a value.)
0331                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-BASE)/256   ; 0 = first page, 1 = second
0331                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-BASE)/256   
0331                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-BASE)/256   
0331                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-BASE)/256   
0331                NPG1:     EQU   21 + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
0331                          IF   (1-TABP0)*(1-PTLATE)   
                    PTAB:        
                              ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
                              DB   h_store & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_str & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_num & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_print & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_and & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_open & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_close & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_add & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_div & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_key & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_def & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_break & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_or & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_not & 0FFh   
                    PTABEND:      
0331                          ENDIF      
0331                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
0331                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
0331                             ; return with the carry clear.
0331   0A           HEXC:     LD   A,(BC)   
0332   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
0334   FE 0A                  CP   10   
0336   38 09                  JR   C,hc1   
0338   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   
033A   D6 11                  SUB   11h   
033C   FE 06                  CP   6   
033E   D0                     RET   NC   
033F   D6 F6                  SUB   0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
0341   03           HC1:      INC   BC   
0342   C9                     RET      
0343                             ; psgn: print HL as a signed number. Keeps BC.
0343   CB 7C        PSGN:     BIT   7,H   
0345   28 04                  JR   Z,pdec   
0347   3E 2D                  LD   A,"-"   
0349   EF                     RST   28h   
034A   E7                     RST   20h   
034B                             ; pdec: print HL unsigned, by recursion on HL / 10 (the stack holds digits).
034B                             ; Keeps BC.
034B   11 0A 00     PDEC:     LD   DE,10   
034E   CD A5 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = HL / 10, E = the last digit
0351   7B                     LD   A,E   
0352   F5                     PUSH   AF   
0353   7C                     LD   A,H   
0354   B5                     OR   L   
0355   C4 4B 03               CALL   NZ,pdec   
0358   F1                     POP   AF   
0359   C6 30                  ADD   A,"0"   
035B   EF                     RST   28h   
035C   C9                     RET      
035D                             ; (The table goes here instead in the builds where, before psgn, it would
035D                             ; cross a page: PTLATE.)
035D                          IF   (1-TABP0)*PTLATE   
035D                PTAB:        
035D                          ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
035D   9A                     DB   h_store & 0FFh   
035E   A2                     DB   h_str & 0FFh   
035F   B7                     DB   h_num & 0FFh   
0360   AD                     DB   h_print & 0FFh   
0361   92                     DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
0362   37                     DB   h_and & 0FFh   
0363   B4                     DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
0364   13                     DB   h_open & 0FFh   
0365   1B                     DB   h_close & 0FFh   
0366   58                     DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
0367   2E                     DB   h_add & 0FFh   
0368   D3                     DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
0369   26                     DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
036A   94                     DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
036B   6C                     DB   h_div & 0FFh   
036C   90                     DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
036D   99                     DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
036E   3F                     DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
036F   4E                     DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
0370   40                     DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
0371   BB                     DB   h_key & 0FFh   
0372   0E                     DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
0373   EA                     DB   h_def & 0FFh   
0374   DD                     DB   h_break & 0FFh   
0375   D9                     DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
0376   72                     DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
0377   85                     DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
0378   C3                     DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
0379   2C                     DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
037A   7A                     DB   h_or & 0FFh   
037B   1C                     DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
037C   82                     DB   h_not & 0FFh   
037D                PTABEND:      
037D                          ENDIF      
037D                             ; =============================================================================
037D                             ;  Console layer. rawk is the host's key routine: a waiting key in A (zero
037D                             ;  flag clear), or A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. putc
037D                             ;  (RST 28h) prints A. Both keep BC, DE, HL and HL'. In the generic build
037D                             ;  they are the host's KEY and CONOUT routines themselves.
037D                             ; 
037D                             ;  A running program reads the keyboard only through getk and pollk, which
037D                             ;  between them give the break key its rules:
037D                             ;    - Ctrl-C stops the program;
037D                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
037D                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
037D                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
037D                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
037D                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
037D                             ;  Both are called straight from a handler, never from a routine under one:
037D                             ;  the checked build's report counts on finding one return address above the
037D                             ;  data stack.
037D                             ; =============================================================================
037D                          IFN   CPM   
037D                RAWK:     EQU   KEY   
037D                          ENDIF      
037D                             ; pollk: the break check (see rpushn).
037D   CD 06 FF     POLLK:    CALL   rawk   
0380   C8                     RET   Z   ; no key
0381   32 7A 82               LD   (KEYBUF),A   ; held for the next "?"
0384   FE 03        PK1:      CP   3   ; (getk joins here)
0386   C0                     RET   NZ   
0387                             ; ctlc: Ctrl-C has been read. If the break key is on, that is the end. If
0387                             ; the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one more key: a
0387                             ; second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the newest wins),
0387                             ; and the Ctrl-C goes to the program: returns A = 3, zero flag clear.
0387   3A 7B 82     CTLC:     LD   A,(BRKOFF)   
038A   B7                     OR   A   
038B   CA 13 04     CT0:      JP   Z,brk   
038E   D5                     PUSH   DE   
038F   11 10 27               LD   DE,250*MSLOOP   
0392   CD 06 FF     CT1:      CALL   rawk   
0395   20 05                  JR   NZ,ct2   
0397   1B                     DEC   DE   
0398   7A                     LD   A,D   
0399   B3                     OR   E   
039A   20 F6                  JR   NZ,ct1   
039C   D1           CT2:      POP   DE   ; A = the second key, or 0 if none came
039D   FE 03                  CP   3   
039F   28 EA                  JR   Z,ct0   ; (the zero flag takes the JP there)
03A1   B7                     OR   A   
03A2   28 03                  JR   Z,ct3   
03A4   32 7A 82               LD   (KEYBUF),A   
03A7   3E 03        CT3:      LD   A,3   
03A9   B7                     OR   A   
03AA   C9                     RET      
03AB                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 and the zero flag if there is none.
03AB   E5           GETK:     PUSH   HL   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
03AC   21 7A 82               LD   HL,KEYBUF   ;   the buffer
03AF   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
03B0   36 00                  LD   (HL),0   
03B2   E1                     POP   HL   
03B3   B7                     OR   A   
03B4   C0                     RET   NZ   
03B5   CD 06 FF               CALL   rawk   
03B8   C8                     RET   Z   
03B9   18 C9                  JR   pk1   ; Ctrl-C? If not, that is the key
03BB                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    BRK:      EQU   endprog   ; the unchecked build stops without a word
03BB                          ENDIF      ;   (with the editor, both stacks are cleared);
03BB                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
                    BRK:      EQU   edit0   
03BB                          ENDIF      
03BB                          IF   CHECKED   
03BB                BRK:      EQU   e_break   ;   the checked build reports B
03BB                          ENDIF      
03BB                          IF   CPM   
                    RAWK:     LD   A,0FFh   ; BDOS 6 with E = FFh: a key, or 0
                                 ; putc: BDOS 6 for every character. BDOS 2 would check for ^S while
                                 ; printing and could swallow a key that BDOS 6 then never sees.
                    PUTC:     PUSH   DE   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              LD   E,A   
                              LD   A,6   
                              CALL   bdosx   
                              POP   HL   
                              POP   DE   
                              OR   A   ; (for getk)
                              RET      
                                 ; bdosx: call BDOS function A with DE, keeping BC and HL'
                    BDOSX:    PUSH   BC   
                              EXX      
                              PUSH   HL   
                              EXX      
                              LD   C,A   
                              CALL   BDOS   
                              EXX      
                              POP   HL   
                              EXX      
                              POP   BC   
                              RET      
03BB                          ENDIF      
03BB                             ; =============================================================================
03BB                             ;  Checked build: the checks and the error report
03BB                             ; =============================================================================
03BB                          IF   CHECKED   
03BB                             ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
03BB                             ; The data stack is right when SP lies in the 256 bytes below DSTOP: adding
03BB                             ; the constant carries if it is above (cells were popped that were never
03BB                             ; pushed), and leaves a high byte of FFh if it is in range. Errors are found
03BB                             ; a character late at most: the bytes above DSTOP and the guard band below
03BB                             ; the page take what happens meanwhile. DE is free between characters.
03BB   EB           CHKSTK:   EX   DE,HL   
03BC   21 05 7E               LD   HL,(1-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; (SP is 2 lower here: the call)
03BF   39                     ADD   HL,SP   
03C0   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
03C1   38 1D                  JR   C,e_under   
03C3   14                     INC   D   
03C4   20 16                  JR   NZ,e_over   
03C6   D9                     EXX      ; the return stack: in its page (or it has
03C7   7C                     LD   A,H   ;   overflowed), and not above its empty
03C8   FE 80                  CP   RSPAGE   ;   position (an underflow stays inside the
03CA   7D                     LD   A,L   ;   page, in the guard band)
03CB   D9                     EXX      
03CC   20 0B                  JR   NZ,e_rover   
03CE   FE E1                  CP   RSTOP&0FFh+1   
03D0   D8                     RET   C   
03D1   D9                     EXX      ; return stack underflow: it counts as empty
03D2   2E E0                  LD   L,RSTOP&0FFh   ;   (H is right: the pointer is in its page)
03D4   D9                     EXX      
03D5   3E 72                  LD   A,"r"   
03D7   18 3C                  JR   errp   
03D9   3E 52        E_ROVER:   LD   A,"R"   ; return stack overflow
03DB   11                     DB   11h   ; (LD DE,nn hides the next entry)
03DC   3E 53        E_OVER:   LD   A,"S"   ; data stack overflow
03DE   18 35                  JR   errp   
03E0   31 FC 81     E_UNDER:   LD   SP,DSTOP   ; data stack underflow: it counts as empty
03E3   3E 73                  LD   A,"s"   
03E5   18 3E                  JR   error   
03E7                             ; e_hi: the inner loop read a reserved byte, 80h-FFh: X. But a word cell that
03E7                             ; was never defined still holds 0000h, and the byte there is a reserved one
03E7                             ; in every build (AFh or C3h): if the IP is in page zero, this was a call of
03E7                             ; an undefined word. The call is undone, so the place is the call itself.
03E7   04           E_HI:     INC   B   
03E8   10 33                  DJNZ   e_resv   ; (B is as it was, and is not 0)
03EA   CF                     RST   08h   
03EB   42                     LD   B,D   
03EC   4B                     LD   C,E   
03ED   3E 55                  LD   A,"U"   
03EF   18 34                  JR   error   
03F1                             ; chkhp: HL = the new heap top, DE = the old one, the carry is from adding
03F1                             ; the count. Stop if the top is not below the limit page, or is below the
03F1                             ; program's end.
03F1                CHKHP:       
03F1                          ENDIF      
03F1                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                                 ; With this much room a top that wrapped round can land back in
                                 ; range, so the add is tested too: growing (A, the count's high
                                 ; byte, is positive) must not carry, and releasing must.
                              RRA      ; the carry comes in above the sign:
                              ADD   A,40h   ;   bit 7 = carry XOR sign
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   C,e_heap   
                              LD   A,(0007h)   
                              DEC   A   
                              CP   H   
                              JR   C,e_heap   
03F1                          ENDIF      
03F1                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
03F1                             ; (Here the program's space is under 32K, so a top that wrapped
03F1                             ; round always falls outside it.)
03F1   7C                     LD   A,H   
03F2   FE F0                  CP   HEAPLIM   
03F4   30 09                  JR   NC,e_heap   
03F6                          ENDIF      
03F6                          IF   CHECKED   
03F6   D5                     PUSH   DE   
03F7   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
03F8   2A 38 82               LD   HL,(NPEND)   
03FB   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; carry: at or above the program's end
03FC   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
03FD   D1                     POP   DE   
03FE   D8                     RET   C   
03FF   B7           E_HEAP:   OR   A   ; put the count back in TOS for the report
0400   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
0402   3E 48                  LD   A,"H"   
0404   18 0F                  JR   errp   
0406                             ; chkst: stop unless HL is in the program's own space: from the letter page
0406                             ; up to the heap limit (the OS, or HEAPLIM), so the interpreter's stacks and
0406                             ; whatever lies above the limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but
0406                             ; below the limit is the program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there.
0406                             ; It is the page of HL + 1 that is tested, so that one test serves both
0406                             ; bytes of a cell: the last byte below the limit can"t be stored to with ".'.
0406                             ; Keeps HL and BC. It runs on into its own error entry.
0406   23           CHKST:    INC   HL   
0407   7C                     LD   A,H   
0408   2B                     DEC   HL   
0409   FE 82                  CP   LETPAGE   
040B   38 03                  JR   C,e_store   
