04E2                          ENDIF      
04E2                             ; =============================================================================
04E2                             ;  The line editor (EDITOR = 1)
04E2                             ; 
04E2                             ;  The interpreter starts here, and a program that ends comes back here.
04E2                             ;  There is no prompt. It follows the spec's suggested standard for a line
04E2                             ;  editor (docs/b8script.md, Environments). Type a line and press Return:
04E2                             ; 
04E2                             ;    n text    put the text in as line n; the lines from n on move down. A
04E2                             ;              number past the end (or 0) adds the line at the end.
04E2                             ;    n         take line n out
04E2                             ;    anything else is run at once, as B8Script. (Start such a line with a
04E2                             ;    space if it would begin with a digit.)
04E2                             ; 
04E2                             ;  A command key ends the line too, and takes what was typed as its argument:
04E2                             ; 
04E2                             ;    ^G        run the program
04E2                             ;    n ^L      list from line n (no number: all of it). Any key holds the
04E2                             ;              list until another key is pressed; Ctrl-C ends it.
04E2                             ;    n ^E      put line n in the input line; Return puts it back, changed
04E2                             ;    name ^R   read. CP/M: the file of that name (no name: the same file as
04E2                             ;              last time). Generic: what is typed, or pasted, from now until
04E2                             ;              ^Z replaces the program; it is not echoed.
04E2                             ;    name ^W   write. CP/M: to that file (no name: the same file as last
04E2                             ;              time). Generic: the text is printed, as it is.
04E2                             ;    ^N ^N     new: no program (the key twice in a row)
04E2                             ;    ^X        leave (to LEAVE)
04E2                             ; 
04E2                             ;  In the line: ^B and ^F, or the left and right arrow keys, move the cursor;
04E2                             ;  a character goes in at the cursor; Backspace and DEL take out the one
04E2                             ;  before it; Esc drops the line. Only CR, LF, BS and printing characters are
04E2                             ;  sent to the terminal, so any terminal will do.
04E2                             ; 
04E2                             ;  Lines are counted, not numbered: the text holds no line numbers, and the
04E2                             ;  list shows each line's place. There can be 65535 lines. A typed line holds
04E2                             ;  125 characters; the one character after a line number separates it from
04E2                             ;  the text and is not stored. The text is kept as it is typed, each line
04E2                             ;  ending in CR LF, at PROG.
04E2                             ; 
04E2                             ;  What lasts from one line to the next: the program, the words, the
04E2                             ;  variables and the data stack. An error or a break clears both stacks. The
04E2                             ;  return stack starts empty for every line.
04E2                             ; 
04E2                             ;  Things to know:
04E2                             ;    - Reset empties the program (generic builds).
04E2                             ;    - A word's address points into the program, so run the program again
04E2                             ;      after editing it.
04E2                             ;    - Nothing is printed between a program's output and what is typed next.
04E2                             ;    - A line run at once sits in the line buffer, which -n? also reads into:
04E2                             ;      a line that calls -n? and carries on afterwards runs what was typed.
04E2                             ;      (The stored program never comes back to the line, so it may.)
04E2                             ;    - The editor"s own keys are not the program"s: -n? is the plain line
04E2                             ;      read of the other builds.
04E2                             ; 
04E2                             ;  The data stack is the CPU's stack, so the editor works on top of whatever
04E2                             ;  the last line left there, with TOS pushed like the rest.
04E2                             ; =============================================================================
04E2                          IF   EDGEN   
04E2                INIT:        ; reset (A = 0)
04E2                          ENDIF      
04E2                          IF   EDGEN*CHECKED   
04E2                             ; Clear the lower half of the letter page: every variable starts at 0, and
04E2                             ; every word cell holds 0000h, the address an undefined word is caught at
04E2                             ; (see e_hi).
04E2   21 00 82               LD   HL,LET   
04E5   77           INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
04E6   2C                     INC   L   
04E7   F2 E5 04               JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
04EA                          ENDIF      
04EA                          IF   EDGEN   
04EA   18 36                  JR   edit0   
04EC                          ENDIF      
04EC                          IF   EDITOR   
04EC                             ; ^F, right arrow: one to the right, by printing the character there
04EC   7D           RIGHT:    LD   A,L   
04ED   BB                     CP   E   
04EE   28 4A                  JR   Z,ed1   ; at the end
04F0   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
04F1   2C                     INC   L   
04F2   18 2B                  JR   lf1   
04F4                             ; Esc: alone it drops the line. An arrow key sends Esc [ and a letter, so
04F4                             ; wait about 5 ms for a second key: after a "[" read on to the letter that
04F4                             ; ends the sequence, and act on C (right) and D (left).
04F4   01 C8 00     ESC:      LD   BC,5*MSLOOP   
04F7   CD 06 FF     ES1:      CALL   rawk   
04FA   20 0A                  JR   NZ,es2   
04FC   0B                     DEC   BC   
04FD   78                     LD   A,B   
04FE   B1                     OR   C   
04FF   20 F6                  JR   NZ,es1   
0501   CD 6F 05               CALL   fin   ; no second key: the line is dropped
0504   18 22                  JR   edit   
0506   FE 5B        ES2:      CP   "["   
0508   20 30                  JR   NZ,ed1   ; not a sequence known here
050A   CD C8 05     ES3:      CALL   ekey   
050D   FE 40                  CP   40h   
050F   38 F9                  JR   C,es3   ; (its parameters)
0511   D6 43                  SUB   "C"   
0513   28 D7                  JR   Z,right   
0515   3D                     DEC   A   ; "D"?
0516   20 22                  JR   NZ,ed1   ; no: on into left
0518                             ; ^B, left arrow: the cursor goes one to the left
0518   7D           LEFT:     LD   A,L   
0519   87                     ADD   A,A   
051A   28 1E                  JR   Z,ed1   ; (L = 80h: at the start)
051C   2D                     DEC   L   
051D   3E 08                  LD   A,8   
051F   EF           LF1:      RST   28h   
0520   18 18                  JR   ed1   
0522                             ; edit0: reset, an error or a break: both stacks are cleared.
0522                             ; skend: a program that ended inside skip: its return address goes.
0522                             ; edend: a program that ended: TOS joins the rest of the data stack.
0522   31 FA 81     EDIT0:    LD   SP,DSTOP-2   ; empty (the cell that stands for TOS is pushed)
0525   21                     DB   21h   ; (LD HL,nn: steps over the next two bytes)
0526   D1           SKEND:    POP   DE   
0527   E5           EDEND:    PUSH   HL   
